---

# What you have

- *Git repository* [${repo_name}](${repo_html_url}) on STACKIT Git (Forgejo), initialized from
  `${repo_clone_addr}`.
- *One project per stage*, each with one namespace on the SKE cluster.
- *One Forgejo Connector per stage*. It gives the repository's pipeline access to that stage's
  namespace and shows the links *Application* and *Pipeline*.

| Stage | Project | Application | Pipeline |
|-------|---------|-------------|----------|
%{ for stage in stages ~}
| ${title(stage.name)} | `${stage.project_name}` | [${stage.app_hostname}](https://${stage.app_hostname}) | [`pipeline.yaml`](${pipeline_url}) |
%{ endfor ~}

# How deployment works

Each stage deploys from the branch of the same name. A push to a branch runs the pipeline, which
builds the `${app_name}` image and deploys it to the namespace of that stage:

%{ for stage in stages ~}
- Push to `${stage.name}` → deploys to ${title(stage.name)}
%{ endfor ~}

The pipeline already ran once per stage, so the application is live.

# Git access

Your access to the repository follows your role in the workspace:

| Workspace role | Repository permission |
|----------------|-----------------------|
| Workspace Owner | admin |
| Workspace Manager | write |
| Other members | read |

1. *Sign in once* to [STACKIT Git](${forgejo_host}) with SSO. The next run of the
   @buildingblock[${git_repository_uuid}] building block adds you to your team. Its summary
   lists who has access.
2. *Add your SSH public key once* in [your Forgejo settings](${forgejo_host}/user/settings/keys).
3. *Clone* the repository:
   ```bash
   git clone ${repo_ssh_url}
   ```

# Manage access

Invite team members in meshStack:
